   },
   "skos:definition": "The presumptive argument pattern \"case C1 is similar to case C2; conclusion A holds in C1; so A plausibly holds in C2\". Its strength depends on whether the shared features are relevant to A, whether relevant differences undercut the comparison, and whether a rival analogy points the other way.",
