    "standard-form categorical syllogism"
   ],
   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "ct:syllogism"
   },
   "skos:definition": "A deductive argument made of exactly three categorical propositions (two premises and a conclusion) using exactly three terms, each appearing twice; its form is fixed by its mood and figure, and validity depends on that form alone.",
