     "@id": "ct:inductive-reasoning"
    },
    {
     "@id": "ct:scientific-method"
    }
   ],
   "skos:definition": "The principle that a statistical association between two variables does not by itself show that one causes the other, because the pattern can also arise from a common cause, reverse causation, selection of the sample, or chance; causal conclusions need further evidence and explicit assumptions.",
