    "De Morgan rules",
    "De Morgan's rules"
   ],
   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "ct:propositional-logic"
   },
   "skos:definition": "The pair of logical equivalences stating that denying a conjunction is the same as asserting that at least one conjunct is false, and denying a disjunction is the same as asserting that every disjunct is false: not-(P and Q) equals not-P or not-Q, and not-(P or Q) equals not-P and not-Q.",
   "skos:inScheme": {
