   "skos:definition": "Aristotle's two-book treatise (c. 350 BCE) that founded formal logic: it classifies two-premise deductions into three figures, proves the imperfect ones by reducing them to a handful of self-evident first-figure moods, shows invalidity by counterexample, and extends the system to necessity and possibility.",
