   },
   "skos:definition": "The ancient puzzle in which a chain of individually plausible small steps (\"removing one grain cannot turn a heap into a non-heap\") leads by valid reasoning from a clearly true starting point to a clearly false conclusion; it arises from tolerant, vague predicates and tests how logic should handle borderline cases.",
