    "Aristotelian square",
    "logical square",
    "traditional square of opposition"
   ],
   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "ct:categorical-proposition"
   },
   "skos:definition": "A diagram that arranges the four categorical statement forms (A, E, I, O) at the corners of a square and labels the logical relations between them: contradictories, contraries, subcontraries and subalterns, which together license immediate inferences from the truth or falsity of one statement to the others.",
   "skos:inScheme": {
