   "rdfs:label": "William J. McGuire",
   "skos:altLabel": [
    "W. J. McGuire",
    "William James McGuire"
   ],
   "skos:definition": "American social psychologist (1925-2007), long at Yale, who in the early 1960s proposed inoculation theory: beliefs can be made resistant to persuasion by exposing people to weakened attacks and refuting them in advance, the idea behind today's prebunking of misinformation.",
