   "rdfs:label": "Zeno of Elea",
   "skos:altLabel": "Zeno the Eleatic",
   "skos:definition": "Greek philosopher from Elea in southern Italy (born c. 490 BCE), a younger associate of Parmenides, known for paradoxes of plurality and motion such as Achilles and the tortoise; he argued by deriving absurd consequences from an opponent's own assumptions, and Aristotle reportedly called him the inventor of dialectic.",
